  "messages": "Maya (Product): Quick thread: re: onboarding first-run flow prototype in staging. Attaching flow GIF: https://redwood-internal.s3/onboard/gif-v3.mp4. Need fast feedback on: 1) info density on the setup checklist, 2) label language for sample projects, 3) keyboard-only path. Low-risk changes this sprint.\nDiego (Design): I pushed a simplified checklist \u2014 3 items instead of 5: 'Connect API key', 'Create project', 'Run sample'. Less friction. Visual hierarchy: bold step number, compact helper text.\nRina (DevEx): Love the 3-step approach. One ask: when user completes 'Connect API key' we should surface the SDK snippet inline so they can copy-paste without leaving the flow. Also add `Copy` button with tooltip.\nJon (Frontend): Implementation detail: inline code block with a copy button is straightforward. Example: `<pre><code>npm install @redwood/infer</code></pre>` + Copy button. Make sure code block has `tabindex=0` so keyboard users can focus.\nPriya (A11y): A11y notes: code block focus is good. Ensure tooltip appears on focus and hover. For the checklist, use <ul> with `role=\\\"list\\\"` and each step is a `<button>` or anchor depending on action so screen readers get it as actionable. Also ensure color contrast of step icon backgrounds meets 3:1 for non-text, and text contrast >=4.5:1 for body copy.\nMaya (Product): For sample projects, current options are: 'Quick chat (streaming)', 'Embeddings search', 'Reranker demo', 'Data connector sample'. Which order? We want to highlight low-friction wins for new users.\nDiego (Design): Order suggestion: 1) Quick chat (streaming) \u2014 shows streaming + chat UI, 2) Embeddings search \u2014 demonstrates semantic search, 3) Data connector \u2014 shows integrations (S3), 4) Reranker \u2014 more advanced. Also tweak labels to use present tense verbs: 'Try streaming chat' / 'Try semantic search'.\nRina (DevEx): Analytics: emit `onboard.step.complete` with `step_name` and `project_choice`. Also track `onboard.banner_shown` + `banner_variant`. We'll A/B the sample project order for 2 weeks.\nJon (Frontend): Microcopy suggestion for the 'Run sample' CTA: 'Launch sample' vs 'Run sample'. Shorter is better. Also include microcopy under the CTA: 'No infra, built-in datasets' \u2014 maybe 'No infra, demo data included'.\nPriya (A11y): Microcopy: prefer 'Demo data included' (clearer). Also ensure links open in same tab unless they go to external docs \u2014 then use `rel=\\\"noopener\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\"` and a visible external link icon.\nMaya (Product): Keyboard-only flow: can we make the entire checklist navigable with arrow keys and Enter to activate? Maybe add skip-link to the main action. Important for power users.\nJon (Frontend): Arrow-key navigation is doable if we render steps as a toolbar role and manage `aria-selected`. But beware of mobile screen readers; implement only for desktop widths.\nDiego (Design): Visual focus state: 3px inset ring with accent color and increased step scale (1.02) on focus. Priya, okay?\nPriya (A11y): Inset ring is ok if contrast is sufficient. Scale animation should be instantaneous (no motion) or provide a 'reduce motion' preference respect. Also ensure focus isn't hidden behind the top nav when stepping through.\nRina (DevEx): PR plan: I'll open a small PR with the reordered sample projects, copy updates, analytics events, and a small SDK snippet embed. Tagging @Jon for keyboard behavior and @Priya for final a11y check.\nMaya (Product): Timeline: aim for a staging deploy tomorrow. If we get quick thumbs, we'll include this in next week's rollout.\nci-bot: Staging build scheduled for 2026-03-24T02:15:00Z (build #4860) after PR merge.\nJon (Frontend): I'll start working on keyboard nav today. Expect a couple of small follow-ups on focus traps.\nDiego (Design): I'll finalize the microcopy variants for the A/B test and drop them in the PR.",
